course: dictionary
lesson: 9877
title: One word, many jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Tackle is a good example: it can be a move in a game, a way of dealing with a hard job, or a set of equipment. The words around it tell you which meaning fits.
explain: Look for clues. «A reckless tackle, like sliding in studs up from behind, is a foul» has the words foul and reckless, so tackle means a move to win the ball in a game. «We tackle the ball, not people» shows that tackling means trying to win the ball.
explain: Then check by swapping in a simple meaning. «Tackle the hardest question first» means start dealing with it, and that fits. Your meaning should always make the sentence sound sensible.
fact: Tackle can be a verb: to tackle, tackles, tackled, tackling.
fact: Tackle can be a noun: a tackle, or tackle as the equipment for a sport, such as fishing tackle.
fact: In sport, a fair tackle goes for the ball, not the player's legs, so nobody gets hurt.
fact: «Tackle» can mean to start dealing with a problem or a hard job, such as tackle your homework.
fact: Phrases to remember: «a sliding tackle», «fishing tackle», «a tackle box», «tackle a problem».
exercise: «A reckless tackle, like sliding in studs up from behind, is a foul.» What does tackle mean here? | A friendly hug after the game | *A move to try to win the ball from a player | A set of fishing rods and hooks | A way of tidying up a messy room
exercise: Maddie made a rule: «we tackle the ball, not people». What does tackle mean in her rule? | *Try to win the ball | Count carefully | Hide from | Throw away
exercise: Tom says, «I will tackle my hardest maths sum first.» What does tackle mean? | Lose interest in | Catch a fish | Hit a ball hard | *Start dealing with a hard job
test: Dad packed his fishing tackle, rods and hooks, into the car. What is tackle in this sentence? | Cooking pots | A kind of weather | *The equipment for a sport | A type of car
test: «The police officer tackled the thief and held him still.» What does tackled mean? | Thanked | Ran away from | Waved at | *Grabbed and stopped
exam: Which sentence uses tackle to mean a move to win the ball in a sport? | *«She made a fair tackle and won the ball back.» | «He bought new fishing tackle for the lake.» | «The tackle box was full of hooks.» | «She will tackle her homework after tea.»
